# Jingle bells - Amerikaans winter- en kerstlied
# Geschreven door James Lord Pierpont, uitgegeven in 1857 als "The One Horse Open
# Sleigh" (Oliver Ditson & Co., Boston), volgens Wikipedia (en), "Jingle Bells".
# Publiek domein. Het laatste couplet staat volgens dat artikel niet in de tekst
# van 1857; het is een latere toevoeging van onbekende herkomst.
# Overgenomen uit JINGLEBE.LLS (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Het refrein staat in de bron
# twee keer achter elkaar en is zo overgenomen. Akkoorden volgens de kolommen; "Gmi"
# van de bron als Gm, en "B6" als Bb6: in F is dat de vierde trap (Duitse notatie B).
{title: Jingle bells}
{meta: id jingle-bells}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: James Lord Pierpont}
{composer: James Lord Pierpont}
{year: 1857}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit JINGLEBE.LLS (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); schrijver en jaar via Wikipedia (en)}
{meta: tag kerst}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse}
[F]Dashing thro' the snow
in a one [Bb6]horse open sleigh
And [Gm]over the fields we [C7]go
laughing all [F]the way
[F]The bells on bobtail ring
making spirits [Bb6]bright
what [Gm]fun it [C7]is to rid[F]e
and sing [Gm]a sleighing song [F]tonight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Jingle bells, jingle bells,
jingle all the way
[Bb6]O what fun it is to [F]ride
in [G7]a one horse open [C7]sleigh
[F]Jingle bells, jingle bells,
jingle all the way
[Bb6]O what fun it is to [F]ride
in [G7]a one horse open [F]sleigh
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
A day or two ago
I thought I'd take a ride
And soon Miss Fannie Bright,
Was seated by my side
The horse was lean and lank
Misfortune seemed his lot
He got into a drifted bank
And we, upset we got
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Now the ground is white
Go it while you're young
Take the girls tonight
And sing this sleighing song
Just get a bobtailed bay
Two forty for his speed
Then hitch him to an open sleigh
And crack! you'll take the lead
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
